{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1221780-found-a-cheeky-nephandi-detector","id":1221780,"title":"Found a cheeky Nephandi detector","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-05-24T11:44:54-07:00","id":1221780,"title":"Found a cheeky Nephandi detector","content":"Mages can get Spirits to do stuff for them. They can ask nicely, or force them, depending on their personality and traits. Regardless of the means, it is possible for a Mage with the Spirit Sphere to acquire the assistance of a Pattern Spider. If I had to describe Pattern Spiders simply, I'd say low-level zero imagination static drones which fortify order in the Umbra, culminating around Technocracy labs and cities and skyscrapers.<br /> <br /> There is a Charm Pattern Spiders may use, called Calcify. This Charm binds a mortal in webs which harden, draining physical Attributes of the Spider's choice. If you hit 0 in any Attribute you're stuck, completely immobile until someone frees you.<br /> <br /> This Charm never works on a Mage who has 4+ in the Entropy Sphere, or is a Marauder, or is a Nephandi, because their dynamism or entropy are too great for such a static power to hold them. Presumably this would also extend to Mages who had fallen into Jhor or a Dynamic Quiet, but I digress.<br /> <br /> In any case, detecting Marauders with outward (that is, ones that go beyond simple perception) Quiets, especially those of 2 or higher, isn't that difficult. And Mages who have a strong understanding of Entropy will give off a certain resonance. So if you apply this Charm to a Mage, the likelihood of a false positive isn't that high. The odds of a Mage having Entropy 4 or greater, or being a Marauder, without that already being obvious, are quite slim.<br /> <br /> The main problem here are false negatives. If the Mage is a Euthanatos Mage of considerable experience, you will immediately conclude that the test won't be worth much there, since they have likely developed an entropic magickal style.<br /> <br /> Regardless, I think it's interesting that this is technically mechanically possible, even if hogtying a potential Nephandus and dragging them into the Umbra so that a Pattern Spider you've tricked into helping you can determine whether they're a Nephandus or not is pretty inconvenient.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 05-24-2018, 02:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T12:42:49-07:00","id":1221802,"title":"","content":"Well, there's yet another thing Nephandi must contend with to be good infiltrators, one wonders how they manage...However, in my personal opinion, I don't think Nephandi should have a lot of problem with this one.<br /> Among other things, it's not very nice to order spirits to attack fellow mages. Mages don't trust mages that much, and thus defending violently against such a &quot;test&quot; should be fairly safe - it's not the kind of things courts would accept as part of the proceedings...especially when it isn't a foolproof method.<br /> <br /> Also, I think Nephandi may already have a counter:<br /> <br /> Ressonance detection it's fairly basic magick. You can do that with Spirit 1 or Mind 1. A Nephandi that doesn't know how to hide his Ressonance it's raising a red flag - Entropy 4 it's OK but Jhor is not, and Jhor it's usually detected by sensing the bad vives the mage constantly emanates.<br /> <br /> There are spells that can hidde Ressonance, but what has this to do with &quot;being too entropic for calcification&quot;?<br /> <br /> Being &quot;too entropic&quot; is covered in M20 by the concept of Synergy. Now, the &quot;Entropic Synergy&quot; it's little more than Ressonance that comes from the outside, formed by the way you interact with the cosmic principle of Entropy. Synergy was what Revised called Ressoance, and the two are still very close (while Resonance it's the world's answer to your manipulations, Synergy it's a response from the Triad).<br /> <br /> It stands to reason that you can hide your Synergy the same way you can hide your Ressonance (after all, Revised had at least one rote to hide Ressonance, and Ressonance in Revised it's M20's Synergy), and any acomplished Nephandi should have one.<br /> This would be a useful trick even without spiders involved, just to be able to invoque the lords of hell in your room that's next to the Chorister's room <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ...if the supression it's enough to fool magick senses, I don't see why such a feat can't erase or diminish the weakness of Calcification, that seems to be more of a broad weakness to certain Synergy/Ressonance than a specific immunity of Nephandi.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 05-24-2018, 03:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T12:54:39-07:00","id":1221805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1221780-found-a-cheeky-nephandi-detector?p=1221802#post1221802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It stands to reason that you can hide your Synergy the same way you can hide your Ressonance (after all, Revised had at least one rote to hide Ressonance, and Ressonance in Revised it's M20's Synergy), and any acomplished Nephandi should have one. This would be a useful trick even without spiders involved, just to be able to invoque the lords of hell in your room that's next to the Chorister's room <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ...if the supression it's enough to fool magick senses, I don't see why such a feat can't erase or diminish the weakness of Calcification, that seems to be more of a broad weakness to certain Synergy/Ressonance than a specific immunity of Nephandi.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, that makes a lot of sense. If a Nephandus is using Prime/Spirit/Entropy to cover up how badly fucked up their Avatar and Resonance are, then that might mean they have no resistance to the powers of Pattern Spiders...<br /> <br /> That's actually a really good answer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T14:34:41-07:00","id":1221841,"title":"","content":"Just another thing to point out, pattern spiders are probably one of the more difficult spirits to command, especially at the lower levels, because they do t really understand the concept of individuality. To a pattern spider all mages are one and the same, part of a whole that acts to undermine the work of the weaver.<br /> <br /> It might be possible to gain the favour of one, but using that favour will be limited to what the spider is capable of, and knowing one mage from another might be a bit beyond it. Jaglings might be a bit easier to instruct, but then harder to command or strike a deal with, and anything greater than that is probably asking for trouble.<br /> <br /> Generally speaking, pattern spiders make good spy drones, help with access to gadgets, making wards and fighting on the defence. But beyond that they tend to be rather limited, especially when on their own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T14:51:46-07:00","id":1221848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1221780-found-a-cheeky-nephandi-detector?p=1221841#post1221841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just another thing to point out, pattern spiders are probably one of the more difficult spirits to command, especially at the lower levels, because they do t really understand the concept of individuality. To a pattern spider all mages are one and the same, part of a whole that acts to undermine the work of the weaver.<br /> <br /> It might be possible to gain the favour of one, but using that favour will be limited to what the spider is capable of, and knowing one mage from another might be a bit beyond it. Jaglings might be a bit easier to instruct, but then harder to command or strike a deal with, and anything greater than that is probably asking for trouble.<br /> <br /> Generally speaking, pattern spiders make good spy drones, help with access to gadgets, making wards and fighting on the defence. But beyond that they tend to be rather limited, especially when on their own.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like they're pretty unique.<br /> <br /> For a Pattern Spider, doing them a favour is giving them work to do. Which is... I mean admirable work ethic. But for a pattern spider, showing them a problem to fix is a great way of utilizing them.<br /> <br /> And so honestly Spirit 2 might be the worst way of manipulating them. Just mess around with them using illusions, and perhaps Spirit 4 to just force them to play along.<br /> <br /> I feel like with all spirits, there is a fundamental problem. The easier they are to control, and safely manipulate, the less powerful they tend to be. A Gnosis 10 Spirit makes the most powerful servant and fetish, but even with Willpower 10 and Spirit 5 that's begging for trouble. A Rage 10 Spirit makes for the most powerful watchdog, but if you lose control of it for even a single round it can murder you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T16:09:17-07:00","id":1221866,"title":"","content":"Don't forget that Pattern Spiders are part of a hive mind. Whatever you tell one is carried back to the rest, while attempting to control one will alert the others immediately. It's very dangerous to force a pattern spider into anything lest the whole cavalry will start hunting for you.<br /> <br /> As for favour, pattern spiders are not as easily placated as you make them out to be. They do not want or desire except to carry out the will of the Weaver, to preserve the web and grow its influence. Even if you do something which aids them in their goal, their inability to recognise an individual makes it difficult for them to acknowledge you as responsible. To have a proper attempt at chiminage with a pattern spider, it will need to be with a jagling at least.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T16:16:34-07:00","id":1221872,"title":"","content":"Err doesn't that kind of conflict with the official mage module that has a specific named pattern spider that's made a deal with the Technocracy to do Technocracy/Weaver Stuff and control the outpouring of wyld energy in San Francisco? (At least I think it was san francisco. Could be elsewhere.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T17:01:59-07:00","id":1221882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1221780-found-a-cheeky-nephandi-detector?p=1221872#post1221872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Err doesn't that kind of conflict with the official mage module that has a specific named pattern spider that's made a deal with the Technocracy to do Technocracy/Weaver Stuff and control the outpouring of wyld energy in San Francisco? (At least I think it was san francisco. Could be elsewhere.)</div> </div> </div> </div>If they had a specific named pattern spider, chances are it was a Jaggling at least.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-25T02:29:27-07:00","id":1221970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1221780-found-a-cheeky-nephandi-detector?p=1221866#post1221866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't forget that Pattern Spiders are part of a hive mind. Whatever you tell one is carried back to the rest, while attempting to control one will alert the others immediately. It's very dangerous to force a pattern spider into anything lest the whole cavalry will start hunting for you.<br /> <br /> As for favour, pattern spiders are not as easily placated as you make them out to be. They do not want or desire except to carry out the will of the Weaver, to preserve the web and grow its influence. Even if you do something which aids them in their goal, their inability to recognise an individual makes it difficult for them to acknowledge you as responsible. To have a proper attempt at chiminage with a pattern spider, it will need to be with a jagling at least.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like M20 frames this slightly differently. It points out that they struggle to recognize Mages (since individuality isn't a concept for them), but it says you can earn their favour by bringing them to a place where they need to work. Now if what you want is for some Wyrm or Wyld / Entropic or Dynamic energies to be stabilized, that's mission complete. But chances are you're having them do this so you can then exploit whatever form of &quot;good will&quot; this metal spider has.<br /> <br /> So I can only assume that you can bargain in terms of actions, rather than people.<br /> <br /> &quot;Follow me and help me&quot; isn't a service such a spirit can fulfill. &quot;Follow that Mage and tell me what he does&quot; is many orders of complexity above it. However if you were to say &quot;I know a place which is currently very disordered and is threatening stability in the Umbra, and I could tell you (that is, all Pattern Spiders collectively) where this is so you can get to work. In exchange, could you (one or more Pattern Spiders) go to [Place] and do [Thing]?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 05-25-2018, 05:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-25T03:42:09-07:00","id":1221977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1221780-found-a-cheeky-nephandi-detector?p=1221970#post1221970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I feel like M20 frames this slightly differently. It points out that they struggle to recognize Mages (since individuality isn't a concept for them), but it says you can earn their favour by bringing them to a place where they need to work. Now if what you want is for some Wyrm or Wyld / Entropic or Dynamic energies to be stabilized, that's mission complete. But chances are you're having them do this so you can then exploit whatever form of &amp;quot;good will&amp;quot; this metal spider has.<br /> <br /> So I can only assume that you can bargain in terms of actions, rather than people.<br /> <br /> &amp;quot;Follow me and help me&amp;quot; isn't a service such a spirit can fulfill. &amp;quot;Follow that Mage and tell me what he does&amp;quot; is many orders of complexity above it. However if you were to say &amp;quot;I know a place which is currently very disordered and is threatening stability in the Umbra, and I could tell you (that is, all Pattern Spiders collectively) where this is so you can get to work. In exchange, could you (one or more Pattern Spiders) go to [Place] and do [Thing]?&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Possibly, but it would be a bit iffy. I imagine gaining a pattern spiders favour might offer you safe passage for a time, information that they are aware of, or even audience with higher ranked weaver spirits. Their hive mind makes them incredible scouts since they would in theory have access to knowledge from all over the pattern web. But when it comes to specific locations for specific tasks, it would depend greatly on how things are asked. Pattern spiders would probably not recognise most proper nouns, instead navigating by exact coordinates upon their web in a code only known to them and their associates, such as the killakrakn cockroaches. Similarly, whether they understand the morality of an action outside of doing harm to reality or not is dubious at best. To a pattern spider, all forms of vulgar magic are a threat, regardless of their intention.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}